What it is for: routers, NAS boxes, cheap VPS panels and client machines
where a key is not an option

Why it helps: no more retyping, no password in a note or alias, no
`sshpass` exposing it on the command line

Why this way: sshr is its own askpass and serves the password over a
one-shot socket, never in argv, the environment or a file, only the
password prompt gets it and only once, so a wrong password does not feed
fail2ban
